<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of White Wolf Mountain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">207</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of White Wolf Mountain was fought in 207 in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoning">Liaoning</a> between the forces of the Chinese warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a> and the Wuhuan, who were sheltering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shao">Yuan Shao</a>'s sons Yuan Shang and Yuan Xi. After a hard march through the mountains, Cao Cao's vanguard under Zhang <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> routed the Wuhuan and killed their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tadun">Tadun</a>. The victory secured northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> for Cao Cao, and thousands of Wuhuan were resettled inside the frontier to serve as cavalry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-white-wolf-mountain.jpg" alt="Battle of White Wolf Mountain" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:End_of_Han_Dynasty_Warlords.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
